369 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 88 0 R
/E (At the start of the robotics season, new members rotated through a variety of team tasks so that everyone could gain exposure to the full range of skills required in robotics. This system introduced members to different team roles, encouraged them to step outside their comfort zones, and helped them understand how each part of the team contributes to overall success. The process was guided by veteran members, who provided hands-on instruction and support throughout the season. After this rotation, members were assigned to positions that best aligned with their interests and strengths. Although not everyone could receive their preferred role, due to the need to fill essential team responsibilities, each member gained valuable experience and developed new abilities. Through the guidance of veterans and occasional support from other teams, we built a more skilled, collaborative, and well-rounded crew. In addition, our team maintains a strong culture of mutual support across all areas of work. When one subteam needs assistance, other members step in to help wherever needed. For example, when the mechanical team requires extra hands, members readily contribute their time and effort. Similarly, when the CAD team is evaluating design options, teammates collaborate through research, discussion, and feedback to help identify the most effective solution. This willingness to support one another strengthens both our teamwork and overall efficiency.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
