827 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 96 0 R
/T (Through iteration, we found that a single-motor shooter introduced unnecessary losses and a slower spin-up time. Transitioning to a dual-motor direct-drive design significantly improved response time, torque delivery, and balance, especially during rapid-fire scoring. Extensive compression testing showed that small geometric changes had outsized effects on accuracy and ball behavior. The addition of an adjustable hood allowed us to decouple velocity from trajectory, while integrating Limelight 3A enabled closed-loop vision alignment without increasing shooter height. Overall, prioritizing a low-profile, efficient design resulted in a lighter, faster, and more consistent shooter system.)
/E (Through iteration, we found that a single-motor shooter introduced unnecessary losses and a slower spin-up time. Transitioning to a dual-motor direct-drive design significantly improved response time, torque delivery, and balance, especially during rapid-fire scoring. Extensive compression testing showed that small geometric changes had outsized effects on accuracy and ball behavior. The addition of an adjustable hood allowed us to decouple velocity from trajectory, while integrating Limelight 3A enabled closed-loop vision alignment without increasing shooter height. Overall, prioritizing a low-profile, efficient design resulted in a lighter, faster, and more consistent shooter system.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
