895 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 97 0 R
/T (Through iterative testing and on-field trials, we learned that traditional kicker-based transfer systems significantly limit scoring speed and efficiency. Kickers can be mechanically complicated and introduce unavoidable delays due to retraction time, timing sensitivity, and inconsistent energy transfer between shots. In contrast, our continuous transfer and rapid-fire system enables a smooth, uninterrupted flow of artifacts, allowing multiple shots to be taken in quick succession without pausing or resetting the mechanism. This shift dramatically reduced cycle time, improved scoring consistency, and better matched the fast-paced nature of gameplay. As a result, we prioritized continuous motion, compliant wheel transfer, and automated gating over discrete kickers.)
/E (Through iterative testing and on-field trials, we learned that traditional kicker-based transfer systems significantly limit scoring speed and efficiency. Kickers can be mechanically complicated and introduce unavoidable delays due to retraction time, timing sensitivity, and inconsistent energy transfer between shots. In contrast, our continuous transfer and rapid-fire system enables a smooth, uninterrupted flow of artifacts, allowing multiple shots to be taken in quick succession without pausing or resetting the mechanism. This shift dramatically reduced cycle time, improved scoring consistency, and better matched the fast-paced nature of gameplay. As a result, we prioritized continuous motion, compliant wheel transfer, and automated gating over discrete kickers.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [32]
>>
